1
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
"Not Yours"

2
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:00,800
(Episode 2)

3
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:29,319
Sorry about that, sir.

4
00:01:29,640 --> 00:01:30,760
That spot is a bit ticklish.

5
00:01:33,079 --> 00:01:35,200
Finally found your weak spot.

6
00:01:37,239 --> 00:01:38,239
Sir,

7
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:39,999
could you skip that spot?

8
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,016
Work somewhere else, please.

9
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:42,040
Thanks.

10
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:43,760
Sure.

11
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:45,400
You got it.

12
00:01:45,439 --> 00:01:47,920
You're the one who
asked for somewhere else.

13
00:01:55,879 --> 00:01:56,879
Young man,

14
00:01:57,400 --> 00:01:59,000
your leg muscles are pretty solid.

15
00:01:59,239 --> 00:02:00,679
You must hit the gym a lot.

16
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:02,359
I don't really work out that much.

17
00:02:03,599 --> 00:02:04,798
Yeah, right.

18
00:02:04,799 --> 00:02:06,438
You don't get muscle
tone like that without lifting.

19
00:02:06,439 --> 00:02:07,560
What a poser.

20
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:09,919
One look at your legs
and I can tell you train hard.

21
00:02:10,159 --> 00:02:11,159
Don't kid a kidder.

22
00:02:11,639 --> 00:02:14,879
Maybe it's because I was
a sports major in college.

23
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:43,719
A sports major, huh?

24
00:02:44,199 --> 00:02:45,560
So was I back in the day.

25
00:02:46,159 --> 00:02:47,400
What a coincidence!

26
00:02:49,159 --> 00:02:51,519
Still, it's pretty common for
sports majors to change careers.

27
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:53,038
A lot of my classmates

28
00:02:53,039 --> 00:02:54,959
went from paying
customers to service providers.

29
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:58,319
I guess they know
better where the aches are

30
00:02:58,680 --> 00:02:59,960
and can really target the spots.

31
00:03:03,759 --> 00:03:05,599
All right, please turn over.

32
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:07,960
Let me help you thoroughly loosen up.

33
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:09,840
Sounds good.

34
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:12,879
Works out, since I've been dancing all day.

35
00:03:14,319 --> 00:03:15,759
My body is aching.

36
00:03:21,879 --> 00:03:24,159
A busy CEO like you

37
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:25,800
still finds time for dance practice?

38
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:27,360
A CEO?

39
00:03:28,719 --> 00:03:29,919
I'm not a CEO.

40
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:32,080
Huh?

41
00:03:32,479 --> 00:03:33,599
You're not the boss?

42
00:03:37,479 --> 00:03:39,959
Hey, brushing against a
sensitive spot happens.

43
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:40,960
We're both guys.

44
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:42,520
No need to make a scene.

45
00:03:42,719 --> 00:03:44,120
I'll switch to another spot, okay?

46
00:03:51,479 --> 00:03:52,159
By the way,

47
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:53,919
why did you just call me a CEO?

48
00:03:54,319 --> 00:03:56,080
Aren't you the boss of Yingyu Group?

49
00:03:56,960 --> 00:03:57,960
No, I'm not.

50
00:03:58,199 --> 00:03:59,199
Who is it?

51
00:03:59,479 --> 00:04:00,960
I'm Master Chen, your masseur.

52
00:04:01,199 --> 00:04:01,840
I'm so sorry.

53
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:02,680
I was held up earlier,

54
00:04:02,759 --> 00:04:03,878
so I'm a bit late.

55
00:04:03,879 --> 00:04:04,360
Shoot.

56
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:05,280
The real masseur is here.

57
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:06,560
Something urgent just came up.

58
00:04:06,639 --> 00:04:08,199
Another masseur will take over for you.

59
00:04:14,686 --> 00:04:16,525
Wait, what did you smear all over...

60
00:06:17,959 --> 00:06:18,759
Bro,

61
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:20,240
Little sister and I already ate.

62
00:06:20,439 --> 00:06:21,560
This is for you.

63
00:06:22,199 --> 00:06:23,199
Don't worry.

64
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:25,240
I'll take good care of
my sister and myself.

65
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:26,680
You don't need to worry about us.

66
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:28,760
Thanks for working so hard, Bro.

67
00:07:21,743 --> 00:07:23,123
[Calling Mom]

68
00:07:25,240 --> 00:07:26,040
We're sorry.

69
00:07:26,041 --> 00:07:28,879
The number you dialed
is temporarily unavailable.

70
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:11,000
It's been so long since
I last saw the stars.

71
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:46,000
Doctor,

72
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:47,999
the young master hasn't had
an allergy flare-up in years.

73
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:49,879
Why did it get so severe all of a sudden?

74
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:52,399
I reviewed Boss P'Eng's recent diet.

75
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:54,255
To look lean on camera for his appearances,

76
00:08:54,279 --> 00:08:55,799
his diet has been far too restrictive,

77
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:58,200
causing malnutrition and
lowering his immune defenses.

78
00:08:58,360 --> 00:08:59,878
He already has a seafood allergy,

79
00:08:59,879 --> 00:09:01,679
specifically to shrimp.

80
00:09:01,759 --> 00:09:03,960
Today's intake was clearly
far past his threshold.

81
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:06,759
We're fortunate we managed
to stabilize him in time.

82
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:12,440
Mingkun.

83
00:09:13,279 --> 00:09:13,919
Young Master.

84
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:15,080
Please just rest.

85
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:16,200
Don't try to speak.

86
00:09:16,639 --> 00:09:17,895
No matter how urgent things are,

87
00:09:17,919 --> 00:09:19,639
it can wait until you're back on your feet.

88
00:09:23,399 --> 00:09:25,120
All right.

89
00:09:26,759 --> 00:09:28,120
Mingkun.

90
00:10:23,559 --> 00:10:24,839
"Regarding compensation,

91
00:10:24,840 --> 00:10:26,080
please get in touch with me.

92
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:27,480
Here is my number.

93
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,120
I am truly sorry.

94
00:10:29,240 --> 00:10:31,320
We never imagined something
like this would happen.

95
00:10:43,759 --> 00:10:45,120
I wonder if that guy is okay.

96
00:10:46,639 --> 00:10:48,159
The driver must have found him, right?

97
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:53,200
Should I call and check?

98
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:00,360
Mr. Mingkun,

99
00:11:00,799 --> 00:11:03,240
Boss P'Eng seems to have an urgent matter.

100
00:11:04,399 --> 00:11:05,519
What else could it be?

101
00:11:05,759 --> 00:11:07,119
He wants to track down that boy again,

102
00:11:07,120 --> 00:11:07,879
demanding to know

103
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:09,775
why he broke his promise
and didn't go back to him.

104
00:11:09,799 --> 00:11:11,239
He even swore the kid is a dead man,

105
00:11:11,519 --> 00:11:13,320
ordering me to locate him tonight.

106
00:11:14,759 --> 00:11:17,440
Anyone who betrays or crosses
him has to pay with their life.

107
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:19,200
Oh.

108
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:25,360
Hello?

109
00:11:26,519 --> 00:11:27,519
Hello.

110
00:11:28,039 --> 00:11:29,639
Is this Mr. Mingkun?

111
00:11:30,399 --> 00:11:31,879
I'm the flower vendor from earlier.

112
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:34,559
Is your boss feeling all right now?

113
00:11:35,279 --> 00:11:36,279
He's fine now.

114
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:37,720
He received proper medical care.

115
00:11:37,879 --> 00:11:38,879
Thank you for asking.

116
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:40,600
Listen...

117
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:42,120
Mr. Pao,

118
00:11:42,159 --> 00:11:43,879
you'd better watch your back lately.

119
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:45,480
Brace yourself for the worst.

120
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:47,319
What do you mean, brace myself?

121
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:48,360
What do you mean by that?

122
00:11:48,960 --> 00:11:50,000
What I mean is...

123
00:11:51,759 --> 00:11:52,999
Just be ready for anything.

124
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,960
I'll do what I can to
smooth things over for you,

125
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:57,360
so try not to stress too much.

126
00:11:58,799 --> 00:12:00,159
Be ready?

127
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:01,600
For what?

128
00:12:02,120 --> 00:12:03,480
That makes zero sense.

129
00:12:05,399 --> 00:12:06,399
Whatever.

130
00:12:06,679 --> 00:12:08,480
I should worry about my own problems first.

131
00:12:09,559 --> 00:12:13,600
When will I ever be powerful like him,

132
00:12:14,039 --> 00:12:15,399
with endless money to burn?

133
00:12:18,399 --> 00:12:20,039
My life is so miserable.

134
00:12:27,320 --> 00:12:28,039
Xiaobei!

135
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:28,960
Xiaobei!

136
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:29,960
Are you home?

137
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:33,879
He's sleeping.

138
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:37,480
Xiaobei!

139
00:12:38,519 --> 00:12:39,519
Xiaobei!

140
00:12:42,399 --> 00:12:42,919
Hurry!

141
00:12:42,919 --> 00:12:43,480
Xiaobei,

142
00:12:43,759 --> 00:12:45,079
wake up!

143
00:12:45,080 --> 00:12:47,080
I've got the craziest,
funniest story to tell you!

144
00:12:47,159 --> 00:12:48,319
What is it?

145
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:50,240
Waking someone up at the crack of dawn...

146
00:12:50,639 --> 00:12:51,279
Come on,

147
00:12:51,559 --> 00:12:52,679
get up!

148
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:54,480
Snap out of it!

149
00:12:55,159 --> 00:12:56,960
Trust me, this is hilarious.

150
00:12:57,120 --> 00:13:00,120
Yesterday, I totally pranked
that narcissistic soy sauce CEO.

151
00:13:01,440 --> 00:13:02,440
Huh?

152
00:13:19,480 --> 00:13:20,895
Why did you prepare so much breakfast?

153
00:13:20,919 --> 00:13:22,279
Didn't I say I'm cutting fat?

154
00:13:22,799 --> 00:13:24,159
Is this portion meant for a pig?

155
00:13:24,360 --> 00:13:25,518
Young Master,

156
00:13:25,519 --> 00:13:27,239
the doctor specifically
emphasized last night

157
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:28,638
that your recent malnutrition

158
00:13:28,639 --> 00:13:30,278
has severely weakened your immune system,

159
00:13:30,279 --> 00:13:31,798
triggering that intense allergic reaction.

160
00:13:31,799 --> 00:13:34,399
He insisted we make sure
you receive adequate nutrition.

161
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:37,279
We don't expect you
to finish everything here.

162
00:13:37,559 --> 00:13:39,000
It's just that...

163
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:41,600
your appetite is like Manchester's weather—

164
00:13:41,799 --> 00:13:42,839
completely unpredictable.

165
00:13:42,840 --> 00:13:45,320
So please, choose
whatever suits your fancy.

166
00:13:45,505 --> 00:13:46,825
You've been by my side this long,

167
00:13:47,320 --> 00:13:48,758
and you still don't know my taste?

168
00:13:48,759 --> 00:13:49,759
Forgive me, Young Master.

169
00:13:52,080 --> 00:13:54,679
I only know your taste in boys.

170
00:13:59,519 --> 00:14:01,278
That flower kid who ran off last night...

171
00:14:01,279 --> 00:14:02,279
Did you find him?

172
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:03,279
Reporting, Young Master.

173
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:05,239
Last night, that Mr. Pao

174
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:06,878
even called to check on how you were doing.

175
00:14:06,879 --> 00:14:08,639
He's clearly terrified by now.

176
00:14:09,039 --> 00:14:11,639
Why not be magnanimous
and let it slide this once?

177
00:14:11,879 --> 00:14:13,878
There's no need to lower
yourself to a street vendor's level.

178
00:14:13,879 --> 00:14:15,639
He's just acting out
of a guilty conscience.

179
00:14:16,080 --> 00:14:17,719
Daring to defy my orders?

180
00:14:17,720 --> 00:14:18,879
He must have a death wish.

181
00:14:19,919 --> 00:14:21,239
If he couldn't get it, he
should've just said so.

182
00:14:21,240 --> 00:14:22,719
Giving his word and then running away?

183
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:24,640
If you were in my shoes,
would you forgive that?

184
00:14:25,200 --> 00:14:26,359
If it were me,

185
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:27,759
I would've simply walked away.

186
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:29,559
Besides, I double-checked.

187
00:14:29,679 --> 00:14:31,600
The alley where you were smoking last night

188
00:14:31,879 --> 00:14:34,639
was barely a hundred meters from our car.

189
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:38,440
I'm not eating.

190
00:14:38,559 --> 00:14:39,696
What kind of garbage is this?

191
00:14:39,720 --> 00:14:41,560
I told you to get a new
chef! Why haven't you?

192
00:14:41,879 --> 00:14:42,879
Young Master,

193
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:44,200
please calm down.

194
00:14:46,200 --> 00:14:47,798
The chef who made this today

195
00:14:47,799 --> 00:14:50,158
is the head chef just brought
in from the Mandarin Oriental.

196
00:14:50,159 --> 00:14:52,398
He was the silver
medalist in the Bocuse d'Or

197
00:14:52,399 --> 00:14:54,319
and took bronze in the
World Golden Chef Awards.

198
00:14:54,759 --> 00:14:58,159
He's already the eighteenth
master chef we've hired for you.

199
00:14:58,240 --> 00:14:59,679
What good are all those awards?

200
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:01,960
I despise pretentious fluff.

201
00:15:02,480 --> 00:15:03,880
I want food meant for human beings!

202
00:15:04,279 --> 00:15:05,759
For actual humans, do you understand?

203
00:15:06,879 --> 00:15:07,999
It seems...

204
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:08,919
you still...

205
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:11,600
prefer the home-cooked meals
Madam used to make for you.

206
00:15:12,480 --> 00:15:13,480
Right?

207
00:15:16,639 --> 00:15:17,639
Take it away.

208
00:15:18,039 --> 00:15:20,039
Just find someone who
can cook to my palate, fast.

209
00:15:20,639 --> 00:15:22,000
And that boy from yesterday—

210
00:15:22,159 --> 00:15:23,439
I want him in front of me today.

211
00:15:24,559 --> 00:15:25,720
I'm going to make him...

212
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:27,480
pay with his life.

213
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:34,440
Hey!

214
00:15:34,519 --> 00:15:35,159
I'm talking to you!

215
00:15:35,159 --> 00:15:36,159
Did you hear me?

216
00:15:36,399 --> 00:15:38,599
Come over here and report
directly to the young master.

217
00:15:40,759 --> 00:15:41,480
Reporting, Young Master.

218
00:15:41,639 --> 00:15:42,320
Understood, sir.

219
00:15:42,639 --> 00:15:44,239
I'll have the stable hands

220
00:15:44,240 --> 00:15:46,000
bring out all five of
our horses right away.

221
00:15:46,240 --> 00:15:47,240
Bring them out for what?

222
00:15:47,559 --> 00:15:48,840
Did I say I wanted to ride?

223
00:15:50,279 --> 00:15:51,359
No, Young Master.

224
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:52,479
Not for you to ride.

225
00:15:52,480 --> 00:15:54,239
They're for that boy.

226
00:15:54,240 --> 00:15:55,080
Once we track him down,

227
00:15:55,081 --> 00:15:57,655
we'll have him drawn and quartered
by five horses, just as you ordered.

228
00:15:57,679 --> 00:15:58,759
Rest assured, sir.

229
00:16:01,759 --> 00:16:02,759
Pardon the interruption, Young Master.

230
00:16:02,760 --> 00:16:04,240
There is an urgent matter to report.

231
00:16:04,519 --> 00:16:05,519
Speak.

232
00:16:06,240 --> 00:16:07,159
Madam's...

233
00:16:07,160 --> 00:16:09,360
The diamond ring left behind by Madam...

234
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:11,000
is gone.

235
00:16:11,001 --> 00:16:12,159
Gone?

236
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:15,678
Isn't it locked in the study's safe?

237
00:16:15,679 --> 00:16:16,559
How could it go missing?

238
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:17,879
It appears...

239
00:16:18,120 --> 00:16:20,359
it was taken by Master Pao, the gardener.

240
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:22,319
Surveillance footage shows
only she entered the study,

241
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:24,080
and she had the key.

242
00:16:24,559 --> 00:16:26,416
She just tends the garden!
How could she have a key?

243
00:16:26,440 --> 00:16:29,200
We're not sure either, sir.

244
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:31,895
Do you know Aunt Pao's whereabouts?

245
00:16:31,919 --> 00:16:33,000
Or her home address?

246
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:34,840
Yes, sir.

247
00:16:35,759 --> 00:16:36,440
Young Master,

248
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:38,119
the top priority right now

249
00:16:38,120 --> 00:16:39,759
is recovering Madam's ring.

250
00:16:40,279 --> 00:16:41,759
Let me dispatch a search party first.

251
00:16:41,879 --> 00:16:42,879
Wait for my word.

252
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:45,638
That jinx from last night
must have cursed me.

253
00:16:45,639 --> 00:16:47,399
Nothing but trouble ever since.

254
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:50,039
Follow me.

255
00:16:50,120 --> 00:16:50,639
Young Master!

256
00:16:50,639 --> 00:16:51,639
Young...

257
00:16:56,360 --> 00:16:57,360
And guess what?

258
00:16:57,679 --> 00:16:59,558
I grabbed the soy sauce
his own company makes

259
00:16:59,559 --> 00:17:01,279
and gave him an "essential oil" massage!

260
00:17:02,039 --> 00:17:03,879
He was drenched in soy
sauce from head to toe!

261
00:17:04,079 --> 00:17:06,039
The soy sauce boss
modeling his own product—

262
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:07,480
priceless!

263
00:17:13,599 --> 00:17:15,279
Don't you think you went a little too far?

264
00:17:15,319 --> 00:17:17,960
He was totally out of line
and bullied you yesterday!

265
00:17:18,599 --> 00:17:19,839
Plus, he called the cops on me!

266
00:17:20,359 --> 00:17:21,799
He had it coming.

267
00:17:21,839 --> 00:17:22,960
Serves him right!

268
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:27,720
How can you be so certain

269
00:17:29,079 --> 00:17:30,239
that he's the soy sauce boss?

270
00:17:30,839 --> 00:17:31,839
Of course he is!

271
00:17:32,279 --> 00:17:32,920
I mean...

272
00:17:33,279 --> 00:17:35,480
His VIP suite was lined
with his company's products.

273
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:37,519
Who else could possibly be that conceited?

274
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:39,119
Then it looks like...

275
00:17:40,599 --> 00:17:41,919
I must've seen a ghost yesterday.

276
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:43,720
What do you mean?

277
00:17:44,119 --> 00:17:45,119
What ghost?

278
00:17:47,119 --> 00:17:49,000
The guy I chased down
in that car yesterday...

279
00:17:49,279 --> 00:17:50,680
He was also the soy sauce boss.

280
00:17:51,720 --> 00:17:53,079
You said you pranked him too,

281
00:17:53,759 --> 00:17:57,558
so between the two "soy
sauce bosses" we ran into,

282
00:17:57,559 --> 00:17:58,640
which one is the real deal?

283
00:17:59,160 --> 00:18:01,120
You didn't mistake someone
else for him, did you?

284
00:18:15,799 --> 00:18:16,920
Wait, what?

285
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:18,759
You ran into the soy sauce boss too?

286
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:21,880
"Works out, since I've
been dancing all day."

287
00:18:23,519 --> 00:18:24,880
"My body is aching."

288
00:18:27,079 --> 00:18:28,838
I think the guy you
messed with yesterday...

289
00:18:28,839 --> 00:18:30,200
might actually be...

290
00:18:31,559 --> 00:18:32,559
Milan.

291
00:18:37,519 --> 00:18:38,759
I knew it!

292
00:18:39,079 --> 00:18:39,920
I was wondering how Milan got so tall

293
00:18:39,920 --> 00:18:40,920
and pale!

294
00:18:41,759 --> 00:18:42,759
What do I do now?

295
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:45,480
Revenge went straight to my head

296
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,440
and I completely lost my senses!

297
00:18:55,160 --> 00:18:56,599
You'd better figure out

298
00:18:56,680 --> 00:18:57,920
what you're going to do next.

299
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:00,616
What do you mean, what am I going to do?

300
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:02,200
It's not like he knows who I am anyway.

301
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:14,000
Don't forget,

302
00:19:14,519 --> 00:19:16,479
upscale places like that
have cameras everywhere.

303
00:19:16,839 --> 00:19:19,118
Oh, please. He'd never
check the security footage.

304
00:19:19,119 --> 00:19:20,119
I know him.

305
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:21,799
He's obsessed with saving face.

306
00:19:22,160 --> 00:19:23,480
He's a celebrity, after all.

307
00:19:24,079 --> 00:19:26,199
Besides, covered in soy sauce

308
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:27,959
and standing outside in his underwear?

309
00:19:27,960 --> 00:19:29,160
How humiliating would that be?

310
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:31,000
He won't.

311
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:32,599
If you say so,

312
00:19:32,759 --> 00:19:33,759
then fine.

313
00:19:34,160 --> 00:19:35,200
If it were me,

314
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:36,839
I'd definitely call the cops.

315
00:19:37,359 --> 00:19:38,440
Call the cops?

316
00:19:38,920 --> 00:19:40,119
Isn't that taking it too far?

317
00:19:41,720 --> 00:19:42,720
Of course not!

318
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:44,000
Think about it.

319
00:19:44,119 --> 00:19:46,159
He doesn't know who your
grudge was really against.

320
00:19:47,160 --> 00:19:49,160
What if you had a hidden camera on you

321
00:19:49,440 --> 00:19:50,799
and leaked the video online?

322
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:52,439
That would destroy his reputation.

323
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:54,200
You always worry over nothing.

324
00:19:54,559 --> 00:19:55,639
He's a complete airhead.

325
00:19:55,640 --> 00:19:56,960
He wouldn't think that far ahead.

326
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:02,320
If he actually goes to the police,

327
00:20:02,359 --> 00:20:03,639
I'll call him Daddy!

328
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:09,118
Daddy!

329
00:20:09,119 --> 00:20:11,880
I want my daddy!

330
00:20:19,160 --> 00:20:20,160
Hurry up!

331
00:20:32,279 --> 00:20:33,279
Here, take this.

332
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:40,200
I want to report a crime!

333
00:20:52,279 --> 00:20:53,720
Leave it to you, Pao Bei.

334
00:20:55,519 --> 00:20:58,000
Your cooking just keeps getting better.

335
00:21:00,359 --> 00:21:01,999
Next time, come over and have them fresh.

336
00:21:02,359 --> 00:21:03,639
These buns were frozen for days.

337
00:21:03,920 --> 00:21:05,400
They don't taste as good reheated.

338
00:21:06,720 --> 00:21:07,319
Bro,

339
00:21:07,319 --> 00:21:08,319
we're heading to school.

340
00:21:09,359 --> 00:21:10,759
I'll walk the kids out.

341
00:21:10,880 --> 00:21:12,518
It's on my way to the police station

342
00:21:12,519 --> 00:21:13,599
to retrieve my lottery box.

343
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:15,696
You're heading to the
restaurant soon, right?

344
00:21:15,720 --> 00:21:16,079
Yeah.

345
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:17,480
Aren't you working today?

346
00:21:17,640 --> 00:21:18,640
I took the day off.

347
00:21:19,119 --> 00:21:20,439
I sold all the flowers yesterday,

348
00:21:20,559 --> 00:21:21,559
so I need to restock.

349
00:21:22,160 --> 00:21:22,640
Sounds good.

350
00:21:22,759 --> 00:21:24,176
I'll meet you at the
night market after work.

351
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:24,640
All right.

352
00:21:24,720 --> 00:21:25,279
See you at the night market.

353
00:21:25,559 --> 00:21:26,039
Let's go.

354
00:21:26,400 --> 00:21:27,000
Say goodbye.

355
00:21:27,001 --> 00:21:28,439
Bye, Bro!

356
00:21:28,440 --> 00:21:28,880
Off we go.

357
00:21:28,880 --> 00:21:29,880
Goodbye!

358
00:21:32,039 --> 00:21:33,039
Come on.

359
00:21:37,960 --> 00:21:39,200
What a dump.

360
00:21:40,240 --> 00:21:41,440
No wonder she steals.

361
00:21:43,319 --> 00:21:44,319
Careful, Young Master.

362
00:21:48,519 --> 00:21:49,640
You said she lives here?

363
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:50,759
Yes, Young Master.

364
00:21:50,760 --> 00:21:52,319
The records point right here.

365
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:54,119
Look,

366
00:21:54,279 --> 00:21:56,399
the unit with the row of
flowers on the terrace is hers.

367
00:21:56,400 --> 00:21:58,000
Playing at romance in a place like this?

368
00:21:58,640 --> 00:22:00,359
Flowers look utterly ridiculous here.

369
00:22:01,559 --> 00:22:02,119
Young Master,

370
00:22:02,359 --> 00:22:04,000
isn't that boy the...

371
00:22:04,519 --> 00:22:05,519
Who?

372
00:22:05,720 --> 00:22:07,118
The flower-selling kid!

373
00:22:07,119 --> 00:22:09,159
The one you said you'd
tear apart with five horses!

374
00:22:09,920 --> 00:22:10,519
I mean...

375
00:22:10,799 --> 00:22:11,920
the kid from yesterday!

376
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:22,720
Talk about rotten luck.

377
00:22:23,480 --> 00:22:24,519
He can't blame me.

378
00:22:25,279 --> 00:22:26,519
He walked right into my trap.

379
00:22:26,960 --> 00:22:29,160
Could he be related to worker surnamed Pao?

380
00:22:30,720 --> 00:22:32,360
Now this just got a lot more interesting.

381
00:22:35,079 --> 00:22:36,119
Stay here, both of you.

382
00:22:36,400 --> 00:22:37,680
I'll handle him myself.

383
00:22:37,880 --> 00:22:39,319
Let me come with you, Young Master.

384
00:22:39,319 --> 00:22:40,039
No need.

385
00:22:40,319 --> 00:22:41,319
I'll deal with him.

386
00:22:42,359 --> 00:22:45,176
Otherwise, it'll look like
I'm ganging up on him.

387
00:22:45,200 --> 00:22:45,960
Hey—.

388
00:22:45,960 --> 00:22:46,960
Young Master!

389
00:23:01,839 --> 00:23:03,358
They can heat them up themselves.

390
00:23:03,359 --> 00:23:04,639
I steamed a big batch this time.

391
00:23:31,960 --> 00:23:33,440
What kind of move is this?

392
00:23:33,920 --> 00:23:35,640
You think you're a Peashooter or something?

393
00:23:36,799 --> 00:23:37,799
What are you doing here?

394
00:23:41,240 --> 00:23:42,680
I'm here to settle the score.

395
00:23:43,440 --> 00:23:44,000
You...

396
00:23:44,001 --> 00:23:46,361
You're trespassing on private
property, I'll have you know!

397
00:23:46,640 --> 00:23:47,920
I can call the police!

398
00:23:49,880 --> 00:23:50,880
Go ahead and call them.

399
00:23:51,920 --> 00:23:52,960
Or should I dial for you?

400
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:55,559
That way, they can haul you off.

401
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:58,440
Why would the police arrest me?

402
00:24:02,839 --> 00:24:04,359
What is the worker Pao to you?

403
00:24:09,200 --> 00:24:10,600
There are lots of people named Pao.

404
00:24:11,319 --> 00:24:13,279
How should I know which
one you're talking about?

405
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:18,119
This Pao.

406
00:24:18,440 --> 00:24:19,440
Your mother.

407
00:24:20,559 --> 00:24:22,535
That's my personal business.
It's none of your concern.

408
00:24:22,559 --> 00:24:23,559
Why do you even care?

409
00:24:30,960 --> 00:24:33,000
Take a look at what your mother did.

410
00:24:34,079 --> 00:24:35,079
My mom?

411
00:24:47,640 --> 00:24:48,680
It's so dark.

412
00:24:49,359 --> 00:24:50,519
Who can even see this?

413
00:24:51,759 --> 00:24:53,279
Keep playing dumb.

414
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:56,119
Let me tell you something.

415
00:24:57,079 --> 00:24:57,839
Your mother,

416
00:24:58,045 --> 00:24:59,045
surnamed Pao,

417
00:24:59,079 --> 00:25:02,679
stole a priceless diamond
ring from my family.

418
00:25:02,680 --> 00:25:03,839
Impossible!

419
00:25:04,359 --> 00:25:05,759
We might not have much money,

420
00:25:06,119 --> 00:25:07,575
but my mom is not that kind of person.

421
00:25:07,599 --> 00:25:08,920
She would never steal!

422
00:25:10,160 --> 00:25:11,440
I'll call her right now and ask.

423
00:25:11,759 --> 00:25:12,759
Just you wait.

424
00:25:17,960 --> 00:25:21,279
The number you dialed is switched off.

425
00:25:27,440 --> 00:25:30,759
The number you dialed is switched off.

426
00:25:44,359 --> 00:25:46,960
These buns are actually delicious.

427
00:25:53,480 --> 00:25:54,679
Don't touch our food!

428
00:25:54,680 --> 00:25:56,200
Get your facts straight.

429
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:58,280
Your mom stole my family's diamond ring.

430
00:25:58,640 --> 00:26:01,000
What's wrong with me eating a bun?

431
00:26:01,640 --> 00:26:03,360
Those are for my little brother and sister!

432
00:26:03,400 --> 00:26:05,255
If you eat them, they
won't have anything left!

433
00:26:05,279 --> 00:26:06,640
I'll pay you.

434
00:26:08,519 --> 00:26:09,680
I don't want your money!

435
00:26:14,759 --> 00:26:15,759
Fine.

436
00:26:20,920 --> 00:26:21,920
Well?

437
00:26:22,279 --> 00:26:23,759
Can't get through, can you?

438
00:26:24,240 --> 00:26:25,600
Her phone is turned off, isn't it?

439
00:26:27,720 --> 00:26:29,559
Her battery must have died.

440
00:26:30,359 --> 00:26:31,960
Keep making excuses.

441
00:26:36,279 --> 00:26:37,519
Won't let me eat your buns?

442
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:39,000
Is that so?

443
00:26:44,559 --> 00:26:45,799
What are you doing?!

444
00:26:46,200 --> 00:26:48,080
Didn't you want to save
them for your siblings?

445
00:26:48,960 --> 00:26:50,680
Then you'll pay off the debt with yourself!

446
00:26:52,319 --> 00:26:53,376
What do you think you're doing?!

447
00:26:53,400 --> 00:26:54,400
Put me down!

448
00:26:54,440 --> 00:26:55,440
I'm not going!

449
00:26:55,480 --> 00:26:56,480
I'm not going!

450
00:26:56,559 --> 00:26:57,559
Put me down!

451
00:26:59,200 --> 00:27:00,160
Put me down!

452
00:27:00,160 --> 00:27:01,160
I won't go!

453
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:03,319
Put me down right now!

454
00:27:04,319 --> 00:27:05,758
Young Master, why are you carrying him out?

455
00:27:05,759 --> 00:27:06,319
Put me down!

456
00:27:06,319 --> 00:27:06,799
Young Master!

457
00:27:07,079 --> 00:27:08,079
I won't go!

458
00:27:08,200 --> 00:27:09,439
Young Master, please put him down!

459
00:27:09,440 --> 00:27:10,440
Put me down!

460
00:27:11,279 --> 00:27:11,799
Put me down!

461
00:27:11,799 --> 00:27:12,200
Young Master,

462
00:27:12,799 --> 00:27:13,839
just put him down first!

463
00:27:17,440 --> 00:27:18,440
You people...

464
00:27:18,519 --> 00:27:20,318
You need to know what
money is clean to make

465
00:27:20,319 --> 00:27:21,400
and what isn't.

466
00:27:21,880 --> 00:27:23,720
If this blows up, you'll be locked up.

467
00:27:24,400 --> 00:27:25,160
Understood.

468
00:27:25,184 --> 00:27:26,184
I'll definitely remember.

469
00:27:27,720 --> 00:27:28,720
Sign the registry over there,

470
00:27:28,721 --> 00:27:29,976
and you can take your things back.

471
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:31,000
Okay.

472
00:27:32,200 --> 00:27:32,799
Name?

473
00:27:33,079 --> 00:27:34,079
Jiang Weibang.

474
00:28:07,519 --> 00:28:08,758
Young Master, please put him down.

475
00:28:08,759 --> 00:28:09,599
Don't exhaust yourself.

476
00:28:09,599 --> 00:28:10,319
Young Master,

477
00:28:10,319 --> 00:28:11,319
there's no need for this.

478
00:28:11,519 --> 00:28:12,519
Young Master!

479
00:28:12,759 --> 00:28:15,039
Put me down!

480
00:28:17,599 --> 00:28:18,720
Careful, Young Master.

481
00:28:20,119 --> 00:28:21,039
Watch your step.

482
00:28:21,039 --> 00:28:22,039
Young Master!

483
00:28:22,119 --> 00:28:22,759
Young Master,

484
00:28:22,760 --> 00:28:24,359
could you please put him down?

485
00:28:24,759 --> 00:28:25,200
Young Master!

486
00:28:25,200 --> 00:28:25,559
Let go of me!

487
00:28:25,559 --> 00:28:26,000
Young Master!

488
00:28:26,480 --> 00:28:27,240
Hurry up!

489
00:28:27,240 --> 00:28:27,759
Let go of me!

490
00:28:27,760 --> 00:28:29,240
I said, let me go!

491
00:28:30,119 --> 00:28:31,319
Let us take him, Young Master.

492
00:28:31,759 --> 00:28:33,159
Don't anyone dare touch him!

493
00:28:33,160 --> 00:28:33,680
Let go of me!

494
00:28:33,680 --> 00:28:34,680
Just try me.

495
00:28:35,480 --> 00:28:37,240
Look at yourself, Young Master.

496
00:28:37,359 --> 00:28:39,535
You barely recovered from
that severe reaction yesterday.

497
00:28:39,559 --> 00:28:40,720
Just let them help—.

498
00:28:41,559 --> 00:28:43,240
Let them carry him in for you.

499
00:28:43,400 --> 00:28:45,719
Why waste your own strength, right?

500
00:28:45,720 --> 00:28:46,920
Get out of my way, all of you!

501
00:28:47,559 --> 00:28:49,839
I handle my own business.

502
00:28:50,799 --> 00:28:51,400
Put me down!

503
00:28:51,400 --> 00:28:51,960
Anyone who stands in my way—.

504
00:28:51,960 --> 00:28:52,759
Won't die!

505
00:28:52,759 --> 00:28:53,759
I won't die!

506
00:28:54,640 --> 00:28:55,640
Go right ahead, sir.

507
00:28:55,641 --> 00:28:56,799
Handle it yourself.

508
00:28:57,640 --> 00:28:58,640
Put me down!

509
00:29:00,839 --> 00:29:01,640
Put me down!

510
00:29:01,640 --> 00:29:02,160
Young Master,

511
00:29:02,160 --> 00:29:02,880
we're already home.

512
00:29:02,881 --> 00:29:04,240
Can't you hear me? Put me down!

513
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:07,400
Do we have a guest?

514
00:29:10,839 --> 00:29:13,319
Put me down!

515
00:29:13,480 --> 00:29:14,639
Brother.

516
00:29:14,640 --> 00:29:16,279
What brings you back?

517
00:29:19,200 --> 00:29:21,758
An artist friend opened an exhibition

518
00:29:21,759 --> 00:29:22,759
and invited me over.

519
00:29:22,960 --> 00:29:24,160
It happens to be nearby,

520
00:29:24,440 --> 00:29:25,559
so I dropped by to see you.

521
00:29:25,960 --> 00:29:27,159
Put me down!

522
00:29:27,160 --> 00:29:28,400
And who is this?

523
00:29:28,720 --> 00:29:29,720
Oh.

524
00:29:33,559 --> 00:29:34,480
Master P'Aya,

525
00:29:34,481 --> 00:29:36,441
this is our new servant
hired to tend the garden.

526
00:29:37,839 --> 00:29:40,000
Hasn't Master Pao always
looked after the garden?

527
00:29:40,400 --> 00:29:42,200
Why hire someone new?

528
00:29:45,119 --> 00:29:45,720
Well...

529
00:29:45,920 --> 00:29:47,080
It's like this, Master P'Aya.

530
00:29:47,839 --> 00:29:49,719
Master Pao had some
personal matters at home,

531
00:29:49,720 --> 00:29:51,038
so she took a few days off.

532
00:29:51,039 --> 00:29:52,838
This is her son.

533
00:29:52,839 --> 00:29:53,759
He grew up around flowers

534
00:29:53,799 --> 00:29:54,815
and knows gardening inside and out,

535
00:29:54,839 --> 00:29:56,920
so we called him in for a few days

536
00:29:57,480 --> 00:29:59,679
so our rare blossoms wouldn't go neglected.

537
00:29:59,680 --> 00:30:00,480
Thank you for stepping in,

538
00:30:00,480 --> 00:30:01,480
young man.

539
00:30:05,160 --> 00:30:07,480
Look at all the dirt on your clothes.

540
00:30:07,519 --> 00:30:09,278
Go upstairs and change into fresh clothes.

541
00:30:09,279 --> 00:30:10,680
Join me for lunch in a bit.

542
00:30:13,200 --> 00:30:14,239
I'll look after the boy.

543
00:30:14,240 --> 00:30:15,479
Leave it to me, Young Master.

544
00:30:15,480 --> 00:30:16,480
Right.

545
00:30:16,759 --> 00:30:17,559
All right.

546
00:30:17,720 --> 00:30:18,720
I'll head upstairs first.

547
00:30:19,599 --> 00:30:20,599
See you in a bit.

548
00:30:25,720 --> 00:30:26,720
Follow me.

549
00:30:27,559 --> 00:30:28,559
Wait.

550
00:30:33,319 --> 00:30:34,319
Wipe your sweat.

551
00:30:39,039 --> 00:30:40,039
Thank you.

552
00:30:41,920 --> 00:30:44,199
How can two brothers from the same family

553
00:30:44,200 --> 00:30:45,960
be like night and day?

554
00:30:46,559 --> 00:30:48,239
This older brother is so gentle.

555
00:30:48,240 --> 00:30:49,240
This way, please.

556
00:31:00,039 --> 00:31:01,039
Jiang Weibang!

557
00:31:02,119 --> 00:31:02,920
I'm doomed.

558
00:31:02,960 --> 00:31:04,598
Please don't realize I'm the masseur

559
00:31:04,599 --> 00:31:06,640
who smothered you in soy sauce last night!

560
00:31:21,440 --> 00:31:22,639
Don't you recognize me?

561
00:31:22,640 --> 00:31:23,640
Jiang Weibang!

562
00:31:24,079 --> 00:31:24,839
You...

563
00:31:24,839 --> 00:31:25,839
You're...

564
00:31:26,759 --> 00:31:28,719
You're my college classmate
Jiang Weibang, right?

565
00:31:30,880 --> 00:31:32,000
Li Milan, right?

566
00:31:32,640 --> 00:31:33,359
Long time no see.

567
00:31:33,360 --> 00:31:34,440
It really is you!

568
00:31:35,119 --> 00:31:37,279
What are the odds of us
running into each other here?

569
00:31:38,359 --> 00:31:40,200
It's broad daylight. Don't be like that.

570
00:31:47,559 --> 00:31:49,919
Why are you dressed so stuffy now?

571
00:31:49,920 --> 00:31:52,039
Weren't you full of
swagger back in the day?

572
00:31:52,880 --> 00:31:54,319
It's called being mature.

573
00:31:54,799 --> 00:31:57,119
You're a celebrity now and
your mouth still has no filter?

574
00:31:57,160 --> 00:31:58,039
Right,

575
00:31:58,119 --> 00:31:58,880
mature.

576
00:31:59,119 --> 00:31:59,640
Hey,

577
00:31:59,839 --> 00:32:01,518
how do I look these days?

578
00:32:01,519 --> 00:32:03,319
Aren't I way hotter than back then?

579
00:32:04,839 --> 00:32:05,920
Nothing special.

580
00:32:08,480 --> 00:32:10,800
The cop just said you got
picked up for selling something?

581
00:32:11,359 --> 00:32:12,359
It's nothing.

582
00:32:12,480 --> 00:32:14,640
Just some contraband.

583
00:32:16,039 --> 00:32:17,559
Seriously?

584
00:32:17,880 --> 00:32:19,759
With your guts, you'd
dare to deal that stuff?

585
00:32:23,279 --> 00:32:26,599
It's not sex toys or something, is it?

586
00:32:28,440 --> 00:32:29,319
And if it is,

587
00:32:29,319 --> 00:32:30,319
do you want some?

588
00:32:31,039 --> 00:32:32,119
If you do,

589
00:32:32,319 --> 00:32:34,079
I'll give you a discount
on the whole stash.

590
00:32:34,359 --> 00:32:35,639
Then open it up and show me.

591
00:32:35,640 --> 00:32:37,295
Let's see if there's anything I could use.

592
00:32:37,319 --> 00:32:38,359
No need to open it.

593
00:32:38,480 --> 00:32:39,160
Trust me.

594
00:32:39,319 --> 00:32:41,039
I guarantee you can use every single piece.

595
00:32:41,440 --> 00:32:43,600
How would I know if I can
use it if I haven't seen it?

596
00:32:44,200 --> 00:32:45,558
Why haven't you changed one bit?

597
00:32:45,559 --> 00:32:46,759
Still treating me like a kid.

598
00:32:46,960 --> 00:32:49,079
What if it really is
contraband like you said?

599
00:32:49,680 --> 00:32:50,680
What if I get arrested?

600
00:32:51,200 --> 00:32:53,400
And you still don't trust
me, just like old times.

601
00:32:53,720 --> 00:32:54,319
Forget it.

602
00:32:54,480 --> 00:32:55,400
I don't have time for this.

603
00:32:55,400 --> 00:32:56,400
I have to get to work.

604
00:32:57,079 --> 00:32:58,079
Hey!

605
00:32:59,799 --> 00:33:01,519
What kind of work are you doing these days?

606
00:33:02,359 --> 00:33:04,295
You're really meddling
in my business, aren't you?

607
00:33:04,319 --> 00:33:06,319
Do I need to report
every job I take to you?

608
00:33:06,720 --> 00:33:07,959
Come on, old classmate.

609
00:33:07,960 --> 00:33:09,558
Don't be such a buzzkill.

610
00:33:09,559 --> 00:33:11,639
I'm just looking out for you.

611
00:33:11,640 --> 00:33:13,960
Old classmate.

612
00:33:17,480 --> 00:33:19,279
I haven't properly introduced myself yet.

613
00:33:19,519 --> 00:33:20,319
My name is Mingkun.

614
00:33:20,480 --> 00:33:21,559
I'm the head butler here,

615
00:33:21,799 --> 00:33:23,599
as well as Master
P'Eng's personal secretary.

616
00:33:24,279 --> 00:33:25,318
If I remember correctly,

617
00:33:25,319 --> 00:33:26,798
your name is Pao Bei, right?

618
00:33:26,799 --> 00:33:27,240
Yeah.

619
00:33:27,559 --> 00:33:28,559
Mr. Mingkun,

620
00:33:29,480 --> 00:33:31,559
he claims my mother stole a diamond ring.

621
00:33:31,960 --> 00:33:33,479
What's really going on?

622
00:33:33,480 --> 00:33:34,879
Just as you've heard,

623
00:33:34,880 --> 00:33:36,358
we reviewed the security footage.

624
00:33:36,359 --> 00:33:38,079
It shows your mother entering the study,

625
00:33:38,400 --> 00:33:40,400
opening the safe, and taking something out.

626
00:33:40,720 --> 00:33:42,599
So we have reason to suspect

627
00:33:42,680 --> 00:33:45,583
that she was the one who took the diamond
ring Madam left for the young master.

628
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:47,000
That's impossible.

629
00:33:47,599 --> 00:33:49,399
My mother would never
do something like that.

630
00:33:49,759 --> 00:33:50,880
She raised us to know

631
00:33:51,519 --> 00:33:52,896
poverty shouldn't break our spirit,

632
00:33:52,920 --> 00:33:54,840
and hardship can never
compromise our integrity.

633
00:33:55,119 --> 00:33:56,599
She would definitely never steal.

634
00:33:56,799 --> 00:33:58,999
Speaking from my personal
relationship with Master Bao,

635
00:33:59,119 --> 00:34:01,399
I don't believe she's the
type to do such a thing either.

636
00:34:01,720 --> 00:34:04,319
However, with the video footage
and her sudden disappearance,

637
00:34:04,839 --> 00:34:07,240
we have no choice but to
treat her as the primary suspect.

638
00:34:07,559 --> 00:34:09,119
Still, please believe me.

639
00:34:09,280 --> 00:34:10,695
We'll get to the bottom of
this as quickly as possible.

640
00:34:10,719 --> 00:34:12,840
If it turns out she had
nothing to do with it,

641
00:34:13,119 --> 00:34:14,919
we will definitely clear
your family's name.

642
00:34:14,920 --> 00:34:16,038
Then please let me go.

643
00:34:16,039 --> 00:34:17,360
Let me go find my mother.

644
00:34:17,840 --> 00:34:20,559
I know she can explain everything to me.

645
00:34:20,960 --> 00:34:22,336
There must be some misunderstanding.

646
00:34:22,360 --> 00:34:23,360
I can't.

647
00:34:23,400 --> 00:34:24,896
Keeping you here was
the young master's order.

648
00:34:24,920 --> 00:34:27,199
I don't have the authority
to simply let you leave.

649
00:34:30,519 --> 00:34:31,280
How about this?

650
00:34:31,440 --> 00:34:32,599
Stay and work here for now.

651
00:34:32,960 --> 00:34:33,800
For one thing,

652
00:34:33,840 --> 00:34:36,039
you'll be finishing your
mother's shift today.

653
00:34:36,119 --> 00:34:38,119
Otherwise, it counts as
an unexcused absence,

654
00:34:38,159 --> 00:34:39,159
and according to the rules,

655
00:34:39,160 --> 00:34:40,320
she would be penalized.

656
00:34:41,760 --> 00:34:42,239
I see.

657
00:34:42,360 --> 00:34:43,360
All right.

658
00:34:43,480 --> 00:34:45,959
I'll cover for my mom and work here today.

659
00:34:45,960 --> 00:34:46,679
Very well.

660
00:34:46,680 --> 00:34:47,840
Thank you for your hard work.

661
00:35:05,440 --> 00:35:06,440
A Pong,

662
00:35:06,760 --> 00:35:08,719
something urgent came
up that I need to handle.

663
00:35:09,039 --> 00:35:11,239
When you're done, could
you cover my shift at the shop?

664
00:35:17,199 --> 00:35:19,719
I have to work at the Chinese restaurant.

665
00:35:19,880 --> 00:35:20,360
Hey,

666
00:35:20,840 --> 00:35:21,840
a Chinese restaurant?

667
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:23,920
It's been forever since
I last had Chinese food.

668
00:35:23,960 --> 00:35:26,039
I'll go support your business today!

669
00:35:28,079 --> 00:35:28,679
This is too heavy.

670
00:35:28,719 --> 00:35:29,320
Let me carry it for you.

671
00:35:29,320 --> 00:35:29,760
Hey!

672
00:35:30,159 --> 00:35:31,279
Who are you looking down on?

673
00:35:31,519 --> 00:35:32,199
Hurry up.

674
00:35:32,480 --> 00:35:33,519
Give it back!

675
00:35:33,679 --> 00:35:35,639
Even if I give it back, do
you even know the way?

676
00:35:36,400 --> 00:35:37,400
Give it back to me!

677
00:35:38,639 --> 00:35:39,639
You're so annoying!

678
00:35:40,239 --> 00:35:41,239
Where is he?

679
00:35:41,679 --> 00:35:42,919
You didn't let him go, did you?

680
00:35:43,000 --> 00:35:43,719
Without your orders,

681
00:35:43,719 --> 00:35:44,719
I wouldn't dare.

682
00:35:44,760 --> 00:35:45,839
He's still in the garden,

683
00:35:45,840 --> 00:35:47,400
finishing his mother's shift for today.

684
00:35:48,440 --> 00:35:49,440
Good.

685
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:52,000
Young Master,

686
00:35:53,360 --> 00:35:55,039
are you going to see him?

687
00:35:55,159 --> 00:35:55,880
What?

688
00:35:55,960 --> 00:35:57,240
Are you trying to stop me again?

689
00:35:57,360 --> 00:35:58,440
I'm not trying to stop you.

690
00:35:58,719 --> 00:35:59,719
It's just that...

691
00:36:00,159 --> 00:36:01,439
Master P'Aya is still here.

692
00:36:01,440 --> 00:36:03,960
And you know the
agreement explicitly stated

693
00:36:04,079 --> 00:36:05,079
that if you...

694
00:36:05,360 --> 00:36:07,079
That agreement again.

695
00:36:08,039 --> 00:36:09,880
Agreement, agreement!

696
00:36:10,159 --> 00:36:11,039
I'm just messing with him.

697
00:36:11,040 --> 00:36:12,360
Why do you keep bringing that up?

698
00:36:12,800 --> 00:36:13,800
Young Master, please.

699
00:36:14,039 --> 00:36:15,399
I'm worried you'll get carried away again.

700
00:36:15,400 --> 00:36:16,558
If you break the rules,

701
00:36:16,559 --> 00:36:17,559
you could...

702
00:36:18,800 --> 00:36:20,960
you could be kicked out of the house!

703
00:36:22,199 --> 00:36:24,718
How could I stand by and
watch you get thrown out?

704
00:36:24,719 --> 00:36:26,118
I can't bear to see you go,

705
00:36:26,119 --> 00:36:27,119
Young Master!

706
00:36:28,599 --> 00:36:29,159
Fine.

707
00:36:29,519 --> 00:36:30,519
I got it.

708
00:36:30,639 --> 00:36:31,639
I know my limits.

709
00:36:33,199 --> 00:36:34,879
Once lunch is ready,

710
00:36:34,880 --> 00:36:35,919
I'll come to your room to let you know.

711
00:36:35,920 --> 00:36:37,280
Why don't you rest here for a bit?

712
00:36:38,639 --> 00:36:39,840
Rest? What for?

713
00:36:40,559 --> 00:36:41,638
I brought him back

714
00:36:41,639 --> 00:36:43,199
just to have some fun, didn't I?

715
00:36:44,599 --> 00:36:45,599
Young Master!

716
00:36:45,920 --> 00:36:46,920
Young Master!

717
00:36:49,920 --> 00:36:52,480
Great. All that acting for nothing.

718
00:37:48,719 --> 00:37:49,719
In broad daylight,

719
00:37:50,000 --> 00:37:52,239
why are you sneaking
up on people like a ghost?

720
00:37:52,599 --> 00:37:53,799
You scared the life out of me!

721
00:37:54,000 --> 00:37:55,000
You little brat.

722
00:37:55,159 --> 00:37:56,159
Such a scaredy-cat.

723
00:37:56,960 --> 00:37:58,199
Who are you calling a brat?

724
00:37:58,559 --> 00:38:00,039
If I'm a brat, you're an old monster!

725
00:38:04,880 --> 00:38:06,600
Excuse me, Young Master. Please step aside.

726
00:38:06,639 --> 00:38:07,840
I need to get back to work.

727
00:38:11,480 --> 00:38:13,119
Please go sit over on that bench.

728
00:38:13,559 --> 00:38:14,199
Stop getting in my way.

729
00:38:14,199 --> 00:38:15,199
I still have a job to do.

730
00:38:37,239 --> 00:38:38,239
Come here.

731
00:38:39,039 --> 00:38:40,039
What now?

732
00:38:40,159 --> 00:38:41,159
Quit talking back.

733
00:38:41,639 --> 00:38:42,639
Come here.

734
00:38:46,639 --> 00:38:47,880
Say whatever you have to say.

735
00:38:48,280 --> 00:38:49,360
I need to get back to work.

736
00:38:49,559 --> 00:38:51,639
I still have a shift at
the restaurant after this.

737
00:38:54,360 --> 00:38:54,679
Don't move.

738
00:38:54,679 --> 00:38:55,079
What are you doing?!

739
00:38:55,280 --> 00:38:56,280
What's wrong with you?

740
00:38:56,800 --> 00:38:57,800
Hold still.

741
00:39:23,800 --> 00:39:24,880
Are you out of your mind?!

742
00:39:25,199 --> 00:39:26,575
The only reason I haven't fought back

743
00:39:26,599 --> 00:39:28,519
is out of respect for
your status as a big boss.

744
00:39:29,840 --> 00:39:31,960
Don't mistake me for a pushover.

745
00:39:32,960 --> 00:39:34,000
If you keep doing this,

746
00:39:34,599 --> 00:39:35,840
I really will hit you back!

747
00:39:39,840 --> 00:39:41,159
Look at you.

748
00:39:41,559 --> 00:39:43,039
Completely ungrateful.

749
00:39:44,079 --> 00:39:45,639
I saw you got pricked by a thorn

750
00:39:46,199 --> 00:39:48,279
and kindly helped disinfect
it to stop the bleeding.

751
00:39:48,960 --> 00:39:50,280
Instead of thanking me,

752
00:39:50,360 --> 00:39:51,440
you threaten to hit me?

753
00:39:52,039 --> 00:39:53,119
It's not a snakebite!

754
00:39:53,280 --> 00:39:55,080
Did you really have
to suck on it like that?!

755
00:40:01,840 --> 00:40:02,840
Besides,

756
00:40:03,239 --> 00:40:04,000
what you pulled on me yesterday—

757
00:40:04,001 --> 00:40:05,521
I haven't even settled that score yet!

758
00:40:05,679 --> 00:40:06,679
Get over here!

759
00:40:07,360 --> 00:40:08,039
Mingkun!

760
00:40:08,039 --> 00:40:08,559
Help me!

761
00:40:09,039 --> 00:40:10,320
Is your boss completely insane?!

762
00:40:11,199 --> 00:40:12,000
Don't worry.

763
00:40:12,119 --> 00:40:13,119
He's just teasing you.

764
00:40:16,320 --> 00:40:18,120
Master P'Aya asked
you to join him for lunch.

765
00:40:20,920 --> 00:40:22,320
Fine. Got it.

766
00:40:25,079 --> 00:40:26,199
After I finish lunch,

767
00:40:26,760 --> 00:40:27,960
we'll keep playing.

768
00:40:40,519 --> 00:40:41,519
Mingkun,

769
00:40:41,760 --> 00:40:44,040
I think there's seriously
something wrong with your boss.

770
00:40:45,599 --> 00:40:46,760
Please just let me go.

771
00:40:46,880 --> 00:40:48,695
I'm genuinely terrified
that when he comes back,

772
00:40:48,719 --> 00:40:49,320
he'll...

773
00:40:49,360 --> 00:40:50,480
try something on me again.

774
00:40:51,840 --> 00:40:52,840
All right.

775
00:40:52,880 --> 00:40:54,400
I'll arrange to send you home shortly.
